RANK: STATECELL-MARGIN-RQ | position=1 | reason=E8 shows the binding constraint is coarse-prefix co-location of behavioural neighbours (K=16 0.3106 vs negatives 0.1352, only 0.0822 at the frozen K=256) and E11 shows the baseline barely beats chance on prefix sharing (0.0907 vs permuted null 0.067); this is the only proposal that scores successor occupancy of each level code (exactly that quantity) as a margin capped by a derived scale tau_l = median nearest-code squared distance, so it can move level-1 membership without overriding reconstruction or reproducing the hyperbolic collapse in E6/E7 (l1_br recall 0.04671, depth-4 prefix survival 0.068, T4 NLL 9.03).
RANK: succframe-warp-rq | position=2 | reason=its per-item warp strength alpha_i from the eigenvalue share of the successor second moment matches the measured heterogeneity in E5 (top-1 successor mass 0.4375 vs 0.0543 across entropy quintiles) and is fully derived with no tuned constant, but the metric is applied as artanh of a warped chord norm, so the curvature is monotone and adds no assignment information (effectively a per-item Mahalanobis warp), and full-rank warping is the class of change E6/E7 show already cost recall (l1_br 0.04671 vs l1_br_euclid 0.06207), so it must clear a higher bar than the bounded margin.
RANK: beh-aniso-poincare-rq | position=3 | reason=its own risk list concedes beta in [0,1] caps the stretch at sqrt(2), and the distance is again a monotone artanh of an anisotropic quadratic form, so curvature carries no extra signal; against E6, where mild geometry-only variants sit at successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500 and tangent_successor_residual 0.05500 versus 0.06207 for the Euclidean assignment, a mild gauge is most likely a no-op inside single-seed noise, and its tangent Frechet codebook update adds an optimisation risk the evidence gives no support for.
RANK: SUCCFRAME-MOEB-RQ | position=4 | reason=the closest existing analogues in E6 are precisely successor-anchored residual/geodesic-path mechanisms and they scored below the Euclidean variant (tangent_successor_residual 0.05500, successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500, successor_geodesic_coarse_v2 0.05463 vs l1_br_euclid 0.06207); it freezes a rank-d SVD of a row-normalised transition matrix before training although E5/E10 show the successor graph is sparse and skew-driven (bin-1 support 2.77, mean out-degree 5.45), so most items get a near-origin popularity-flavoured anchor, and it simultaneously replaces the reconstruction loss with geodesic squared, the confound its own risk list admits one run cannot separate.
OBJECTION: The mechanism I place first can plausibly be a near no-op: the measured behavioural signal is thin (E9 positive vs fixed-negative successor-cohort sharing 0.9291 vs 0.8871; E11 same-first-prefix 0.0907 vs null 0.067), so a margin bounded at one derived quantization unit may move level-1 membership without pushing Stage-3 test_recall@10 past 0.065, and in a programme that trains each candidate once with no ablation arm that outcome would be indistinguishable from seed noise; add that tau_l is frozen at level initialisation from the initial encoder geometry and may no longer match the distance scale after 3000 epochs, and that a failure cannot be attributed between the coupling, the derived constant and the single seed.
